# Exceptions to the secret scan in tools/safe-push.sh.
# One substring per line. A diff line containing any of them is exempt.
#
# Every entry needs a reason. An exception without one is indistinguishable
# from a mistake, and the whole point of listing them here rather than
# loosening the rule is that someone can audit this file.

# ── Solana transaction signatures ────────────────────────────────────────────
# A signature is 64 bytes in base58 — 87 to 88 characters. An ed25519 secret
# key is 64 bytes in base58 — 87 to 88 characters. They are the same shape and
# no regex separates them.
#
# This register exists to publish transaction signatures, so the rule fires on
# exactly the content the repository is for. Listing each signature keeps the
# base58 rule at full strength for everything else, which is what matters: a
# signature published by mistake costs nothing, a key published by mistake is
# the incident this repository documents.
#
# Verify before adding: a signature resolves on an explorer and is already
# public on chain. If it does not resolve, it is not a signature.

